Libmcrypt is a thread-safe library providing a uniform interface
to access several block and stream encryption algorithms.
Check the manual page for more information on libmcrypt.

Look at COPYING for license information and the individual files for more 
information. COPYING applies only for the mcrypt program and not the 
algorithms which most of them are public domain.

**
** Some hints:

Since 2.5.4 libmcrypt does not use dynamic loading for the modules by default.
All the algorithms and modes, are now included in the library. 

**
** Building with CMake:

CMakeLists.txt builds the same static library as libmcrypt.gyp. It is meant
to be pulled into another project, not installed system-wide, because the
mcrypt.h in this tree differs from upstream's (no module directory arguments).

    add_subdirectory(third_party/libmcrypt)
    target_link_libraries(app PRIVATE libmcrypt::libmcrypt)

or, without a copy in your tree:

    include(FetchContent)
    FetchContent_Declare(libmcrypt
        GIT_REPOSITORY https://github.com/tugrul/libmcrypt-gyp.git
        GIT_TAG        <commit>)
    FetchContent_MakeAvailable(libmcrypt)
    target_link_libraries(app PRIVATE libmcrypt::libmcrypt)

Then #include <mcrypt.h>. To build and test the library on its own:

    cmake -S . -B build
    cmake --build build
    ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure

** How the modules are wired together:

Every algorithm (modules/algorithms/*.c) and every mode (modules/modes/*.c)
keeps its functions static and exports one constant structure of function
pointers, its descriptor: mcrypt_algo_rijndael_128, mcrypt_mode_cbc and so
on. lib/mcrypt_registry.h defines the two structure types and declares the
descriptors; lib/mcrypt_registry.c lists the ones mcrypt_module_open() finds
by name.

Upstream gave every module function a name-mangled global symbol instead
(rijndael_128_LTX__mcrypt_set_key) and generated a table of them,
lib/mcrypt_symb.c, at configure time.

3-way, panama, safer-sk64 and safer-sk128 are compiled and have descriptors
but are not listed, as in upstream's default build.
